WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.287
Why treat a one-line rule as code?

2
00:00:02.287 --> 00:00:06.400
Because in this migration,
access follows the HR record.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.275
HR values land in a few coded attributes,

4
00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:14.588
and dynamic rules read them to decide
who gets access, licenses and policy.

5
00:00:14.588 --> 00:00:18.205
Every rule that grants access
starts with two guards:

6
00:00:18.205 --> 00:00:21.575
the account is enabled, and
it's a member, not a guest.

7
00:00:21.575 --> 00:00:26.225
The validation kit from Chapter 3 already
checks the rules live in a tenant.

8
00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:29.892
This chapter moves those checks
earlier, into the pull request,

9
00:00:29.892 --> 00:00:33.550
so a bad rule is caught before
the engine starts moving people.
